{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30029 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Cassialactone appears to exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways that ultimately target CCF-STTG1. The first pathway involves direct targeting of Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is then a target of 5-Oxobrucine and N-Methyltyramine, both of which have CCF-STTG1 as their target. This suggests a cascade of molecular interactions that culminate in the modulation of CCF-STTG1. The second pathway involves Cassialactone directly targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is subsequently targeted by N-Methyltyramine, again leading to CCF-STTG1. The third pathway, while less direct, also shows a clear link between Cassialactone and CCF-STTG1 through a metabolite-like intermediate. These findings collectively indicate that Cassialactone may influence CCF-STTG1 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme inhibition or metabolic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with multiple potential mechanisms contributing to the observed effects. The evidence supports a plausible biological link between Cassialactone and CCF-STTG1, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interactions and their relevance to the disease state.",
